WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.620
- Ladies and gentleman,

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.020
put your hands together,

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.560
and welcome on stage,
the Chairman of VaynerX.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.043
The one and only, Gary Vaynerchuck!

00:00:15.291 --> 00:00:16.810
(audience applause)

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.570
Raise the roof!

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:19.403
Come on!

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:22.183
- Thank you.

00:00:25.198 --> 00:00:27.413
Thank you, thank you.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.320
I love you very much.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.850
Sharjah, I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.050
Thank you for having me.

00:00:36.512 --> 00:00:39.512
(audience applause)

00:00:41.669 --> 00:00:44.090
There's so many things that
I want to cover in this time

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:46.150
so let's just get right into it.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.750
A couple things.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.400
When you grow up the way I did,

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.260
and for a lot of people in
this room that don't know,

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.693
I'll give you the one minute version

00:00:54.693 --> 00:00:57.310
because so much of the
energy I'm feeling here today

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:00.480
across the UAE, and
specifically at this event,

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.870
and on social with my interactions, is,

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.910
I was born in the former Soviet Union

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.690
and then I came to the United States

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.057
when I was three years old.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.100
My father worked every minute.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.620
I really didn't spend
a lot of time with him

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:19.008
until I was 14, 15, when I
worked in the liquor store

00:01:19.008 --> 00:01:22.700
that he started working
at for $2.00 an hour

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:25.668
as a stock boy and eventually
saved all his money

00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:29.230
and bought a store in
Springfield, New Jersey.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:34.230
I was a product of the
1980's, and 1990's in America,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.180
which I think when people look back on

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:40.570
will be the golden era of education

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:44.030
and what college you
went to basically meant

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.410
who you were gonna be in the world.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:50.450
In the face of education
being the only way out

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:53.193
in the 80s and 90s
especially for an immigrant.

00:01:54.741 --> 00:01:56.960
My mother created a framework

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.880
that allowed my to flourish

00:02:00.318 --> 00:02:01.313
against my own DNA.

00:02:02.345 --> 00:02:04.400
My self awareness, who I was,

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.270
which was a D and F student.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.100
The worst grades that
you could get in school

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.797
but also was a child that
on summer day vacations

00:02:14.797 --> 00:02:18.390
or when it snowed, or
whatever was happening,

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:21.220
I was always looking
to be an entrepreneur.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.230
If it snowed in New Jersey,

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.200
I was ringing doorbells looking
to get money to shovel snow.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.950
If it was hot outside,

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:32.160
I was setting up a lemonade
stand to sell lemonade.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.235
From the beginning of my life,

00:02:34.235 --> 00:02:36.441
I was put in a position,

00:02:36.441 --> 00:02:41.006
luckily based on where I was
and who was parenting me,

00:02:41.006 --> 00:02:44.410
to actually lean into my strengths,

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.420
and the things that I
was passionate about.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.410
It's very interesting
what I'm actually thinking

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.820
while I stand here, which is,

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:56.919
here we are 20 years, 30
years later, from that boy,

00:02:56.919 --> 00:03:01.691
where now entrepreneurship
gives me the luxury,

00:03:01.691 --> 00:03:06.227
gives me the honor to come to
all places around the world

00:03:06.227 --> 00:03:09.690
and people treat me with admiration

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.500
and respect and kindness.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.339
Ironically, the explosion
of entrepreneurship,

00:03:16.339 --> 00:03:19.460
and events like this
and movements like this,

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:23.423
don't excite me as much
as most people think.

00:03:23.423 --> 00:03:27.178
I of course, am a student, a product,

00:03:27.178 --> 00:03:31.490
and a humongous advocate
of entrepreneurship.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:35.147
However, that is completely secondary

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:40.147
to my passion around self
awareness and happiness.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:45.585
It is my great concern, that
the framework, the world,

00:03:45.585 --> 00:03:49.087
that has put me on a
pedestal, entrepreneurship,

00:03:49.087 --> 00:03:52.790
is going to blind some of you in this room

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.920
who are actually unbelievably capable

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.830
to be a number two, a number
three, a number seven,

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:01.620
within an organization,

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.090
but believe in the hype,

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:07.070
that the only way to
win, or more importantly,

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:10.500
what's cool now, is to be a founder.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.878
I encourage every single
person here who has the stomach

00:04:14.878 --> 00:04:18.004
and the mindset for entrepreneurship,

00:04:18.004 --> 00:04:21.450
but I implore you, if you take anything

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.340
from my keynote today,

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.920
please go home and look
yourself in the mirror

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.620
and start having unbelievably

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.910
honest conversations with yourself,

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:33.500
about who you are, versus
who you wish you were.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.363
Today entrepreneurship, in 2018, 2019,

00:04:37.363 --> 00:04:40.820
across the world, is put on a pedestal.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:44.700
I promise you, today I walk
into an event like this

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.340
and everybody wants a selfie,

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:49.060
and I get treated this
way, and it's unbelievable,

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:51.110
but I promise you as I stand here,

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:55.100
I am very mentally prepared for 2027,

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.450
when the global economy collapses

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.400
and I start getting blamed

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.420
for teaching or telling
you to do entrepreneurship

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.880
when your startup failed.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.030
For me, this is my life.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.920
When it wasn't cool.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:10.690
Now while it's cool,

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.670
and in a decade when
it won't be cool again.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:15.150
I want that for you,

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:18.180
because when you do what
you were meant to do,

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.790
when you're able to put
two fingers in your ears

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.000
and hear nothing.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.550
Not the hate or the negativity,

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:28.060
but equally, not the
admiration and the accolades,

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.330
you're playing within yourself.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.330
You're playing within yourself.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.760
My great fear,

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:35.420
my great fear around the world

00:05:36.299 --> 00:05:38.700
is how many people here are
not playing for themselves?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.980
They're playing for their parents.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.410
They're playing for their friends.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:46.250
The things they buy,
the things they start,

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.530
the way they live, are predicated

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.300
on other people's opinions.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.150
Not themselves.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:55.278
I'm not coming here to
start with a buzzkill,

00:05:55.278 --> 00:05:58.890
but I also do not want to be delusional

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.660
to the reality of the situation.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:05.240
To build a meaningful company
takes a very long time,

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.360
is very difficult, and more importantly,

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.660
what has happened in
the startup community.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.630
All those wonderful startups back there,

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:17.270
everybody now is pandering
to venture capital

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:18.870
or to raising capital.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:21.280
Not to actually building a business.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.520
Every day.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.353
Thank you.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:25.203
It's important.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.510
Thank you so much for jumping on that.

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:32.040
It's important, because
let me tell you why

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:35.000
in 2006, 2007, 2008, 2009,

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.080
I was taking all of my money

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.730
and investing in Tumblr and Facebook

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:41.170
and Twitter and Uber,

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:43.670
and all these things that
I did very well with,

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.540
and why over the last four years,

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:48.719
I've invested very little, very carefully,

00:06:48.719 --> 00:06:52.250
because there's a disconnect right now,

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:55.050
and there's illusions of the reality.

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:57.520
If you stand here or sit here today

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.610
and there is nothing that
you could think about

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:02.050
other than building a business,

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:04.960
because the process of
building a business,

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.520
is your happiness.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:10.440
Not what a successful
business allows you to buy.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:12.590
Well then you're a pure
bread entrepreneur.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.050
Somebody asked me today in an interview,

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:17.250
what do I do with my downtime?

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.453
I told them that I start other businesses.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:22.330
It's all I know.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:23.423
It's who I am.

00:07:24.546 --> 00:07:26.450
It's the same way when I see a teacher,

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:28.780
or an artist, or anybody.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:31.090
When I can see through their soul,

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:34.530
that they were meant to
cook, or paint, or build,

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:35.780
or whatever it may be.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.273
I get such happiness.

00:07:38.118 --> 00:07:40.650
It's the same reason that people
that I went to school with

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:44.442
who make $53,000 a year,
but I know they're so happy,

00:07:44.442 --> 00:07:46.300
because it's what they want.

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:48.200
They want to be home at 5:00 PM.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.420
They want to be on multiple sports teams.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:52.470
They want every weekend off.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.363
They don't want the pressure.

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:57.250
Let me talk about pressure real quick.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:59.400
Can I tell you why I stand here

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.040
in this incredible event,

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.500
where entrepreneurship is
being put on this pedestal,

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.760
something I dreamed of my whole life,

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.550
that would eventually be cool,

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.970
and I start my conversation

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:12.520
with heavy levels of practicality,

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:15.580
it is because this is
the thing I most fear.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:19.230
When the last regime, school,

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:23.170
had its day, you could get good grades.

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:24.320
Fake environment.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:26.110
Very easy to manipulate.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.610
You could go work in a company,

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.810
and if that company fired
you or didn't do well,

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:33.970
you had somebody to blame.

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:37.468
You did not have to take
any of the responsibility,

00:08:37.468 --> 00:08:40.374
or have the scarlet letter of losing

00:08:40.374 --> 00:08:42.872
because you were part of a machine.

00:08:42.872 --> 00:08:47.518
The greatest thing about being
a CEO founder entrepreneur,

00:08:47.518 --> 00:08:50.030
is that when there is success,

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:53.805
you get a disproportionate
amount of the credit.

00:08:53.805 --> 00:08:56.870
The problem with entrepreneurship,

00:08:56.870 --> 00:09:00.810
is when it fails, you
have nobody to blame.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.290
One of the things that
I'm most worried about

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:06.683
is when you are a purebred entrepreneur,

00:09:06.683 --> 00:09:09.123
you don't care about losing.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.450
The process is your religion.

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:16.740
Running the company is your oxygen.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:18.180
When you are not,

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:20.330
and you're doing it for everybody else,

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.820
or because it's cool,

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:25.524
when you fail, you will
have no place to hide,

00:09:25.524 --> 00:09:30.250
and your loss will be very
public and unavoidable.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:34.250
The reason I put so much pressure
on people being self aware

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:39.250
is if you're a natural
number two, six, 13, or 27,

00:09:39.799 --> 00:09:43.214
the negatives of being a number one,

00:09:43.214 --> 00:09:47.713
are overwhelming and very
difficult to quantify.

00:09:47.713 --> 00:09:50.680
You have to ask yourself today,

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:53.430
that when your business fails,

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:57.470
are you okay with the judgment
of your family, friends,

00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:00.810
your social media followers,
and the entire world,

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:04.250
and if you are, then you
can move on your merry way,

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:05.790
but if you are not,

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.660
one of the great ramifications

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:10.280
of this golden era of entrepreneurship,

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:13.460
is going to be the enormous
amount of depression

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:18.210
and mental illness when
99% of the businesses fail.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:19.483
That concerns me.

00:10:20.511 --> 00:10:23.511
(audience applause)

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.270
My friends, please don't misunderstand me.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.590
I don't stand up here and say,

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:32.193
I'm an entrepreneur, you're not.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:37.250
I say, that what this
phenomenon has taught me,

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:40.300
where I can go to the most
amazing places on Earth

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.220
and many people know who I am

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:46.180
is that my timing for
what I loved, worked out.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:47.940
I take no pride in that.

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:50.750
I understand that it's circumstantial,

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.020
but I also know,

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:53.760
that this is why I'm so desperate

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:57.300
for you to stick to your
guns around your passion.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.970
Maybe you actually love
playing video games

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.300
more than starting an app company.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.660
When I was growing up,

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:06.420
playing video games was a waste of time.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:08.620
Today, I think we can all agree,

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:12.380
a professional e-sports
superstar for the next 50 years,

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:15.117
probably behind proper
football and basketball

00:11:15.117 --> 00:11:18.520
is going to be the biggest
athlete in our world.

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:19.950
This is nothing you could see

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.030
seven or 10 years ago.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:25.290
You must, you must,
you owe it to yourself,

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:27.630
to make sure that you're
building a company

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:29.120
around what you love.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:33.450
Not because cryptocurrency
is the current fad.

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:35.740
When you chase money, you lose.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:39.300
Always and forever, even
when you achieve the money.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.160
This is how humans are wired,

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:43.010
and so we have to have dramatically

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.350
more thoughtful conversations,

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:48.390
around entrepreneurship, start up culture,

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:51.200
and what's actually
happening in the world,

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:54.550
because right now, most of the unicorns,

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:58.133
are just rhinoceroses in disguise.

00:11:59.507 --> 00:12:03.321
(audience applause)

00:12:03.321 --> 00:12:05.818
Please don't get it confused.

00:12:05.818 --> 00:12:07.710
I like every other person,

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:09.790
have my selfish wants and needs.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.760
That last statement, that was selfish.

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:15.433
D-Rock, where you at?

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:18.290
I did that right now.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:21.340
The unicorn for
rhinoceroses for one reason.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:25.480
I know that 95% of the
successful internet companies

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:27.380
that we all put on a pedestal,

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:29.700
are so over leveraged,

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:32.140
against the reality of their business,

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:35.230
that when there is an
economic slow down or collapse

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:36.900
and they can't raise capital,

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:40.160
against a ridiculous
valuation, they will disappear.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.690
Not because I'm smart.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:42.853
It's because I'm old.

00:12:44.353 --> 00:12:47.250
The one great thing about being 43,

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:50.163
is I've lived through three collapses.

00:12:50.163 --> 00:12:52.634
A lot of people think.

00:12:52.634 --> 00:12:53.960
How many people here under 32 years old?

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.480
Raise your hands.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.943
Geez.

00:12:56.943 --> 00:13:00.226
(audience laughing)

00:13:00.226 --> 00:13:02.180
The biggest gift and the
biggest vulnerability

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:03.443
is that you're 32.

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.687
The biggest thing that,

00:13:06.687 --> 00:13:08.170
there are so many things
running through my mind.

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:10.480
Number one, one of the
most fascinating things

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:11.680
running through my mind,

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:15.062
looking at the NIMEA area,

00:13:15.062 --> 00:13:17.287
and looking at North
Africa, the Middle East,

00:13:17.287 --> 00:13:18.340
it's devastating to me,

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:20.210
how much of the young talent here

00:13:21.244 --> 00:13:23.210
thinks they need to go to America

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:25.530
or other places to achieve their goals

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:27.953
when there is so much opportunity.

00:13:27.953 --> 00:13:30.420
(audience applause)

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:31.253
I mean it,

00:13:34.232 --> 00:13:36.460
and if you're like me,
and you love your family,

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.680
I wasn't even willing
to move to Los Angeles,

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.020
because I needed to be
close to my mom and dad.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:43.190
The thought of going to
another part of the world

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:46.440
when the disproportionate opportunity

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:50.420
is doubling down on your
region is fascinating to me.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:52.900
It's a credit to the
thing I most care about

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.220
which is brand building.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:57.750
America's great achievement
in the last 100 years

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:01.380
is using Hollywood to build its brand.

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:04.120
Please do not get confused.

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:06.050
There is so much opportunity

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:08.560
within a square mile of your home,

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:11.200
let alone the rest of the region,

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.140
that you do not need to be naive

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.960
and think you need to go
somewhere to achieve your goals,

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:19.660
because I'm jealous that I'm not under 32

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:22.870
sitting here with the outlook that I have.

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:24.890
When you look at the mobile penetration.

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:26.800
The percentage of the youth.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.280
When you just look at
the sheer opportunity

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:33.080
that is in the general
region, it's extraordinary.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.840
Too many people underestimate
what's in front of them

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:38.603
and over estimate what's outside of them.

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:40.847
I mean it.

00:14:40.847 --> 00:14:43.847
(audience applause)

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:47.890
Let's bounce around a little bit.

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:49.730
I'm gonna take it to a
slightly different direction,

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:52.230
because I think it's unbelievably inherent

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:53.823
to so many people in this room.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.340
I generally believe,

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:59.560
and by the way, not
everybody should do video.

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:00.920
Not everybody should do video.

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:03.250
Have somebody following
them around with a camera.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.070
Not everybody should do video.

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:08.380
However, if you're
sitting here in the room,

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:10.899
front row, last person back there,

00:15:10.899 --> 00:15:13.544
if you are not producing content

00:15:13.544 --> 00:15:16.240
for the world on the internet,

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:18.650
whether that's because
you're a tremendous writer,

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:20.790
and you can write on your own blog,

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:24.120
on Medium, on LinkedIn, on Facebook.

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:27.200
Pictures because you're
unbelievably visual.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.540
You can take a beautiful photo

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:31.170
and then write a wonderful
three or four sentences

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:33.130
on your Instagram post.

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:36.215
If you're stunningly
handsome and charismatic,

00:15:36.215 --> 00:15:40.120
and you can do video, please,

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:43.040
but if you are great at talking,

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.340
but uncomfortable in front of a camera

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:48.378
and you have to do audio in podcast form,

00:15:48.378 --> 00:15:53.030
please understand my
biggest truth here today

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:56.066
which is if you are not
sharing your thoughts,

00:15:56.066 --> 00:15:59.795
your process, your journey,

00:15:59.795 --> 00:16:03.092
your progress to achieving your goals,

00:16:03.092 --> 00:16:05.170
the stories you want to tell

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:08.320
about your startup, product, service.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:11.127
If you are not communicating to the world

00:16:11.127 --> 00:16:13.480
and if you're not thinking about

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:15.330
what's valuable to them,

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:16.800
not what's valuable to you,

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:19.350
when you communicate, and
that is a very big point.

00:16:20.524 --> 00:16:21.838
I'll say it one more time.

00:16:21.838 --> 00:16:22.870
If you are not communicating to the world,

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.610
and when you're communicating.

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:27.300
If you're not thinking about
what's valuable to them

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:30.290
versus what you're
putting out for yourself,

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:34.193
you are basically
irrelevant in a 2019 world.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:38.800
As much as it may be difficult
for many in this room,

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:41.682
if you are not living through here,

00:16:41.682 --> 00:16:43.423
you are not known.

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.730
This is the game.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.160
Unfortunately or fortunately,

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:50.090
I don't know how you
see technology advances.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:51.830
I'll surprise you.

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:55.430
I'm not so pro technology revolutions.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:56.843
I'm just practical.

00:16:58.383 --> 00:17:01.840
My friends, at 18 years old,

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:03.570
me, at 18 years old,

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:05.900
had spent less than
two hours on a computer

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:08.020
in my entire life.

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:11.846
I am not fascinated by technology at all.

00:17:11.846 --> 00:17:13.610
3-D printing.

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:16.880
I don't care if you make 80%
of your homes 3D printed.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:18.470
I'm not passionate about that.

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:21.530
VR, AR, Blockchain, all of it.

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:22.900
Not really passionate to me.

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:24.953
I'm passionate about communication,

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:28.410
and that's where this happens.

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:31.010
If you are underestimating this,

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:33.110
and when I say underestimating this,

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:36.770
if you have not made a
significant commitment

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:41.390
to producing content for
the one of seven apps

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:45.780
or websites that 80% of this entire region

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:48.490
spends a disproportionate amount of time

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:51.050
penetrating, and listening, and consuming,

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:54.816
you are becoming vastly,
vastly, irrelevant.

00:17:54.816 --> 00:17:58.030
If you leave with anything from this talk,

00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:01.530
number one, please lean
in to self awareness.

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:04.711
There is so much delusion
running through this conference

00:18:04.711 --> 00:18:07.710
and this region and this world,

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:10.230
it's devastating, because
it will not end well.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:14.350
Number two, once you
establish that self awareness,

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:16.300
you must speak.

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:18.600
Everybody speaks differently.

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.870
Through pictures, words, audio, video,

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.150
but you must speak.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:25.900
You must speak because that is absolutely

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:27.630
the leverage that you sit with.

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:29.640
We're sitting in the time right now

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:31.290
where across this region,

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.540
there's so much opportunity.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:36.260
There's so much attention in a YouTube,

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:39.170
Snapchat, Instagram,
Facebook, Twitter world.

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.500
It's unparalleled.

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:44.750
There's never been a time
where every person in this room

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:46.370
with nobody in the middle,

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:48.820
has the ability to
reach anybody they want.

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:53.040
My friends, actually how many
people over 40 in this room?

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:54.580
Raise your hands.

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:55.413
Over 40.

00:18:58.543 --> 00:19:00.410
I wish, and I'm sure,

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.400
I'm looking at a bunch of you right now.

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:04.220
There is a complete misunderstanding

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:06.630
of the disproportionate opportunity

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.730
that everybody in this room has.

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:11.670
All of us who are over 40 dreams

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.420
that we entered a world
with this many options.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:17.000
We were stuck in the machine,

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.730
where there's one or two paths.

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:20.730
There was no options.

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:23.150
You are crippled by options.

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:26.120
You are crippled by options,

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.280
which now leads me to the most

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:30.483
important part of this conversation.

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:35.110
The number one thing that
I think about every day

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:37.880
is why do people live their lives,

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:39.913
based on other people's opinions?

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:43.320
The number one thing that
I really want to have.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:44.710
How many people here under 30?

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:45.543
One more time.

00:19:46.390 --> 00:19:48.532
Raise your hands.

00:19:48.532 --> 00:19:51.437
The number one thing I wish

00:19:51.437 --> 00:19:53.890
for everybody who just raised their hand,

00:19:53.890 --> 00:19:56.230
is my ability to spend a two hour dinner

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:57.523
with your parents.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:03.700
In that dinner would be the
most interesting insight.

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:05.970
Especially regions like this.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:07.860
It is fascinating how
many people are dealing

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:11.249
with the pressures of what
their parents want them to do.

00:20:11.249 --> 00:20:13.243
Versus what you want to do.

00:20:14.591 --> 00:20:17.591
(audience applause)

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:20.740
Woo is right,

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:21.880
and the reason you're wooing,

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:23.780
and the reason that I'm most fascinated,

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:27.333
is I am fascinated by watching parents

00:20:27.333 --> 00:20:31.404
parent their children in the exact way

00:20:31.404 --> 00:20:35.248
that they hated their
parents parented them.

00:20:35.248 --> 00:20:38.248
(audience applause)

00:20:39.461 --> 00:20:41.430
It's remarkable to watch.

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:44.152
You would think somebody who was forced

00:20:44.152 --> 00:20:46.890
to go to University and become a doctor,

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:49.797
lawyer, engineer, banker,

00:20:49.797 --> 00:20:54.400
all that pain and anguish
that those years created.

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:56.450
You would think that they were capable

00:20:56.450 --> 00:20:58.210
of not repeating it,

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:02.730
but the problem is the
great insight of my life

00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:06.280
is how many parents parent their children

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:11.280
only and 100% based on
what other parents think

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:12.410
about their children.

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:18.030
This is the most important
topic in this region.

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:21.882
In a world, specifically to this region,

00:21:21.882 --> 00:21:25.830
where there is so much opportunity.

00:21:25.830 --> 00:21:28.562
The paradigm shift that is needed

00:21:28.562 --> 00:21:31.320
is one on the parenting level

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:34.110
to create the freedom for children

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:36.510
to be able to become happy.

00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:41.067
Not check the box of what
they're supposed to do.

00:21:41.067 --> 00:21:43.600
(audience applause)

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:47.620
Now, before all the 30
year olds clap and say,

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:50.960
hell yeah Gary, before that,

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:52.580
there's one part of the equation

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:55.530
for all the children that are
so happy with this framework.

00:21:56.550 --> 00:22:00.189
If you take your parents
money, they're in charge.

00:22:00.189 --> 00:22:03.189
(audience applause)

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:07.270
I love to talk about,

00:22:07.270 --> 00:22:08.660
you should go do your thing.

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:10.140
You should live your life for you.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:12.370
I'm passionate and I believe this.

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:14.950
That I much rather most of
you have two or three years

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:16.720
where you're fighting with your parents,

00:22:16.720 --> 00:22:18.970
but then have 50 years of happiness,

00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:20.720
because you're not living with regret.

00:22:20.720 --> 00:22:22.430
I'm passionate about that.

00:22:22.430 --> 00:22:24.830
The problem is, I've been blown away,

00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:28.179
by how many kids think they
can go start their own company

00:22:28.179 --> 00:22:31.183
while their parents pay
for their lifestyle.

00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:36.296
You either live on your
own two feet or you do not.

00:22:36.296 --> 00:22:39.296
(audience applause)

00:22:43.179 --> 00:22:46.893
99% of the startups back there will fail.

00:22:49.730 --> 00:22:52.033
99, 97.

00:22:52.914 --> 00:22:56.870
The amount of people that
ever achieve a business

00:22:56.870 --> 00:22:59.180
that there's a million
dollars a year in revenue

00:22:59.180 --> 00:23:01.303
is almost non existent.

00:23:02.510 --> 00:23:04.210
Yet, we live in a world now,

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:06.290
where everybody thinks 50% of people

00:23:06.290 --> 00:23:08.490
are going to build a
billion dollar company.

00:23:10.730 --> 00:23:15.170
Optimism is foundational
for entrepreneurship.

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:18.020
Unless you are blindly
optimistic of your idea

00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:19.890
you'll never get it off the ground,

00:23:19.890 --> 00:23:21.990
because everything around you will say no.

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:26.610
Delusion is the great vulnerability

00:23:26.610 --> 00:23:29.620
of starts ups and entrepreneurs.

00:23:29.620 --> 00:23:33.830
Being practical and realistic
and being optimistic

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:35.133
is very feasible.

00:23:36.192 --> 00:23:37.770
Unfortunately it is rare.

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:39.620
If I could ask anything,

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:42.523
how many people here have a
startup, or are an entrepreneur?

00:23:43.382 --> 00:23:44.215
Raise your hands.

00:23:44.215 --> 00:23:46.460
If I could ask anything of those,

00:23:46.460 --> 00:23:49.040
please start converting your business

00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:51.710
into something that actually makes money.

00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:54.244
Not is in the need of funding,

00:23:54.244 --> 00:23:56.250
because when you look at the framework

00:23:56.250 --> 00:23:57.970
of what's happening globally,

00:23:57.970 --> 00:24:00.590
we can't survive this much longer,

00:24:00.590 --> 00:24:02.760
being this globally over leveraged,

00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:05.230
and when it falls, it falls hard.

00:24:05.230 --> 00:24:07.780
It fell hard in 2007 and 2008.

00:24:07.780 --> 00:24:08.890
You guys know.

00:24:08.890 --> 00:24:11.470
It fell hard in 2001.

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:13.700
It falls hard and this is the most

00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:15.250
over leveraged we've ever been.

00:24:16.414 --> 00:24:19.700
Please, if you leave with anything,

00:24:19.700 --> 00:24:22.100
besides self awareness,

00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:25.750
please leave with am I
prepared to turn my business

00:24:25.750 --> 00:24:28.380
into something that generates profit?

00:24:28.380 --> 00:24:32.406
Not is checking the box
for the amount of users

00:24:32.406 --> 00:24:35.535
or CAT or LTV, or monthly downloads,

00:24:35.535 --> 00:24:39.419
or all the things that
venture capitalists,

00:24:39.419 --> 00:24:42.330
and funding want you to do.

00:24:42.330 --> 00:24:46.140
In a game where those people
are playing a very simple game.

00:24:46.140 --> 00:24:49.430
You have to understand
what investing is about.

00:24:49.430 --> 00:24:52.381
They need to push every one
of their products very hard,

00:24:52.381 --> 00:24:54.160
because if one gets through,

00:24:54.160 --> 00:24:56.060
it pays for everybody else.

00:24:56.060 --> 00:24:59.160
The problem is if you're
one who got pushed too hard

00:24:59.160 --> 00:25:01.260
and didn't build an actual business,

00:25:01.260 --> 00:25:02.500
you didn't win.

00:25:02.500 --> 00:25:04.010
The fund won,

00:25:04.010 --> 00:25:06.890
because one of the 50 companies did.

00:25:06.890 --> 00:25:10.630
We need a call to practicality.

00:25:10.630 --> 00:25:15.090
We need a call to
practicality in our ecosystem

00:25:15.090 --> 00:25:19.660
because without it, the
outcome is always ugly.

00:25:19.660 --> 00:25:22.780
Also when you've had such
a long period of global,

00:25:22.780 --> 00:25:25.409
and I know there's different
markets and I understand,

00:25:25.409 --> 00:25:27.970
but global prosperity at this level

00:25:27.970 --> 00:25:31.100
without any fiscal accountability.

00:25:31.100 --> 00:25:32.333
Just a matter of time.

00:25:33.560 --> 00:25:37.210
My call this morning, this afternoon,

00:25:37.210 --> 00:25:38.780
is a couple things.

00:25:38.780 --> 00:25:40.550
Is this really the game you want to play?

00:25:40.550 --> 00:25:42.615
Because let me remind you,

00:25:42.615 --> 00:25:43.615
I'm awfully jealous.

00:25:44.517 --> 00:25:48.710
A lot of my friends who are
number three, seven, 20, and 41

00:25:48.710 --> 00:25:51.930
at Facebook and Uber and
all the other companies

00:25:51.930 --> 00:25:53.270
that did well.

00:25:53.270 --> 00:25:57.220
Number two, how practical
is your business?

00:25:57.220 --> 00:26:01.130
Have you succumb to the
jargon of start up world?

00:26:01.130 --> 00:26:04.630
Where everything is about
users and viewability and CAT

00:26:05.767 --> 00:26:07.130
and all these terms that
have nothing to do with

00:26:07.130 --> 00:26:08.580
are you making more money

00:26:09.504 --> 00:26:11.180
than you're losing every month?

00:26:11.180 --> 00:26:13.596
Let me tell you how much talent it takes

00:26:13.596 --> 00:26:17.023
to lose money every month consistently.

00:26:20.520 --> 00:26:21.353
Zero.

00:26:22.190 --> 00:26:26.580
It takes zero talent to lose tens

00:26:26.580 --> 00:26:29.480
if not hundreds of thousands
of dollars every month

00:26:29.480 --> 00:26:31.950
while you're building to your exit.

00:26:31.950 --> 00:26:34.030
It looks good on a chart,

00:26:34.030 --> 00:26:35.793
except the chart isn't real.

00:26:37.051 --> 00:26:38.440
What does that lead me to?

00:26:38.440 --> 00:26:40.323
That leads me to the opportunity.

00:26:41.300 --> 00:26:43.050
I'm gonna get very practical with you.

00:26:43.050 --> 00:26:45.710
If you as a person or you as a business,

00:26:45.710 --> 00:26:48.576
are not buying Instagram story ads,

00:26:48.576 --> 00:26:50.420
in this region right now.

00:26:50.420 --> 00:26:53.090
Right now, in this region, UAE,

00:26:53.090 --> 00:26:55.010
across the Middle East, North Africa,

00:26:55.010 --> 00:26:57.210
if you are not doing
that right this second,

00:26:57.210 --> 00:27:00.190
you are making an enormous mistake.

00:27:00.190 --> 00:27:02.510
I am the bi-product of buying

00:27:02.510 --> 00:27:05.180
under priced ads my whole career.

00:27:05.180 --> 00:27:06.490
My dad's liquor store,

